
    public static int findKthLargest(int[] nums, int k) {

        // Min heap
        PriorityQueue<Integer> minHeap = new PriorityQueue<>();

        for (int num : nums) {

            // Add current number
            minHeap.offer(num);

            // Keep only k largest elements
            if (minHeap.size() > k) {
                minHeap.poll();
            }
        }

        // Heap top = kth largest
        return minHeap.peek();
    }

MOST IMPORTANT INTUITION

Heap never stores all elements.

It only stores:

best k candidates

Small elements get kicked out immediately.

Why Heap Size Exactly k?

Because we only care about kth largest.

If heap grows beyond k:

remove smallest useless element

Complexity
---------------
We process:

n elements

Each insertion/removal:

O(log k)

Total:

O(n log k)

Much better than:

O(n log n)

when k is small.
